## Notes on the bibliography

### Original NLTK references

The entries in this table are derived from the bibliography maintained with the first edition of the NLTK book:

> Bird, Steven, Ewan Klein, and Edward Loper. *Natural Language Processing with Python*. O'Reilly Media, 2009.

NLTK's first-edition bibliography also contains many **journal articles, conference papers, book chapters, corpora, datasets, and software resources**. Those are intentionally not included in this book-only table.

For example, the bibliography contains the article *A Formal Framework for Linguistic Annotation*, the British National Corpus, TIMIT, MaltParser, TLG, and individual chapters from edited volumes. These are references in the NLTK bibliography but are not standalone books.

### Edition preservation

Where possible, the table links to the edition actually cited by NLTK rather than substituting a newer edition.

For example:

* Alpaydin's NLTK citation is the **2004 first edition** of *Introduction to Machine Learning*. MIT Press identifies that edition as ISBN `9780262012119`. [MIT Press](https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262012119/introduction-to-machine-learning/)
* Baayen's *Analyzing Linguistic Data* is the **2008 edition** cited by NLTK and is still listed by Cambridge University Press. [Cambridge University Press](https://www.cambridge.org/highereducation/books/analyzing-linguistic-data/B2AF752A30911F4144CA35E075C6B233)
* Agirre and Edmonds' *Word Sense Disambiguation* is the **2007 first edition** published by Springer. [Springer](https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4020-4809-8)
* Dowty, Wall, and Peters' *Introduction to Montague Semantics* is the **1981 first edition** and remains catalogued by Springer. [Springer](https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-94-009-9065-4)
* Niyogi's *The Computational Nature of Language Learning and Evolution* is the **2006 MIT Press edition** cited by NLTK. [MIT Press](https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262140942/the-computational-nature-of-language-learning-and-evolution/)
* Carpenter's *Type-Logical Semantics* is available from MIT Press as the 1998 paperback edition corresponding to the work cited in the NLTK bibliography. [MIT Press](https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262531498/type-logical-semantics/)

### Link quality

Links are prioritized in this order:

1. Publisher page
2. DOI or institutional record
3. Official author/institution page
4. Google Books bibliographic record

A Google Books link is used when an authoritative publisher page for the historical edition could not be located reliably. It is intended as a **bibliographic lookup**, not as an assertion that the book is freely available.

